# Where the Apex Legends weapon catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-10-01**, during **Season 30: Marked, Split 2**
(Season 30 launched 2026-08-04; Split 2 started 2026-09-15). `catalog.json` in
this folder is every gun a player can pick up in Apex Legends' Battle Royale;
this file says where every fact and every picture in it came from.

**Pictures: publisher pictures only (decision D116).** Every picture in
`weapons/` is Electronic Arts' own image, cut from the eight screenshots of the
game's **Legend Locker weapon screen** on EA's own help site
(help.ea.com, "Apex Legends guns and weapons guide"). So each is the game's
own weapon render, exactly as the game draws it, on that screen's blue
backdrop. None came from a fan wiki, Fandom, wiki.gg, a loadout site or an
image search. They are EA's copyright, used in the app to identify the weapon,
the same risk the owner accepted in D116. Delete a `.png` and set that
weapon's `image` to `null` and the app shows the class symbol instead; nothing
else changes.

## The list

EA's help article **"Apex Legends guns and weapons guide"**
(<https://help.ea.com/en/articles/apex-legends/guns-and-weapons/>, "Updated 2
days ago" when read on 2026-10-01) names every gun class and every gun in it.
Its classes and their order are the game's own: the same as the tabs of the
Legend Locker weapon screen in its screenshots (HAVOC, FLATLINE, HEMLOK, R-301,
NEMESIS for the assault rifles, and so on). The catalog keeps that order.

Counts: **29 guns in 7 classes**: Assault Rifles 5, SMGs 5, LMGs 4, Marksman 4,
Sniper Rifles 4, Shotguns 4, Pistols 3. 8 have an official picture. This is
the same 29 that press write-ups of Season 30 count ("29 weapons total").

Three names differ between EA's help article and EA's newer patch notes. The
catalog uses the patch notes' name, keeps the other as an `aliases` word (so
search finds both) and marks the item `uncertain`:

- **Hemlok Breach AR** (help article: "Hemlok Burst AR"). EA's Marked patch
  notes (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/news/marked-patch-notes>) tune
  the "Hemlok Breach AR" and its Breach Charge. The community wiki says the
  Breach AR took the Burst AR's place in floor loot in Season 28 Split 2
  (2026-03-24).
- **RE-45** (help article: "RE-45 Auto"). The Marked patch notes call it
  "RE-45" and give it an energy stockpile. The community wiki says the
  three-round **RE-45 Burst** (energy ammo) replaced the RE-45 Auto in Season 28
  Split 2. If the owner's screen writes "RE-45 BURST", rename the item (its id
  stays `pistols.re_45`).
- **Bocek Compound Bow** (help article: "Bocek 2.0"). EA's Marked Midseason
  patch notes (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/news/marked-midseason-patch-notes>,
  2026-09-14) call it "Bocek Compound Bow".

**Not in the list, on purpose:** Legend abilities that shoot (Rampart's Sheila,
which is her Ultimate, not a gun you carry), ordnance (grenades, Arc Stars,
thermites), melee (cosmetic in Apex: every Legend punches), and limited-time
mode weapons.

**Akimbo.** The P2020 and the Mozambique Shotgun can be held two at once
("Akimbo"); EA's help article says they take one weapon slot, so they are one
gun each here, not separate entries.

## Care Package and gold weapons

Care Package (supply drop) guns are the same guns as on the floor, moved there
for a season; they are not separate entries, and nothing in the catalog
records the rotation, because it changes every season and the gun's picture
and id do not. For the record, on 2026-10-01: the Marked patch notes move the
**30-30 Repeater** into the Care Package and return the **G7 Scout** to the
floor; press write-ups of Season 30 name the Care Package guns as the
**Kraber .50-Cal Sniper**, the **L-STAR EMG** and the **30-30 Repeater**
(not confirmed by an EA page). Gold weapons are no longer a rotating set
(Marked patch notes, "Gold Weapon Rotation Removed").

## Ammo (`ammo`)

The ammo each gun takes, as `light`, `heavy`, `energy`, `shotgun`, `sniper` or
`arrows` (EA's help article names those types). The C.A.R. SMG takes both
heavy and light. From the community wiki's ammo page
(<https://apexlegends.wiki.gg/wiki/Ammo>), checked against EA's Marked patch
notes, whose energy rework lists the energy guns: HAVOC, Nemesis, Devotion,
L-STAR, RE-45, Volt and Triple Take (energy ammo boxes were removed in Season
30; those guns now carry a regenerating stockpile). A gun in the Care Package
uses "Mythic" ammo that comes with it while it is there; its `ammo` is still
its own type.

