## No official picture (image: null)

EA publishes no clean per-weapon render set: ea.com has no weapons page
(`/games/apex-legends/about/weapons` is a 404), the Marked and Marked
Midseason patch notes show season art and screenshots, not single guns, and
the help article shows only the eight above. The app shows the class symbol
for these until the owner trains the weapon from his own screen, and his crop
then becomes the row's picture (D122 section 5):

- VK-47 Flatline, Hemlok Breach AR, R-301 Carbine, Nemesis Burst AR (group `assault_rifles`)
- Alternator SMG, Prowler Burst PDW, Volt SMG, C.A.R. SMG (group `smgs`)
- Devotion LMG, L-STAR EMG, M600 Spitfire (group `lmgs`)
- G7 Scout, Triple Take, Bocek Compound Bow (group `marksman`)
- Longbow DMR, Kraber .50-Cal Sniper, Sentinel (group `sniper_rifles`)
- EVA-8 Auto, Mastiff (group `shotguns`)
- RE-45, P2020 (group `pistols`)

The fan wikis (apexlegends.wiki.gg, Fandom) carry a render of every gun, but
those are EA's art re-hosted by a fan site, which D116 rules out as a source.
Using them is the owner's call, not this file's.

## Update the list when a season changes the guns

Apex adds or reworks a gun every few seasons, at each season and each
mid-season split. For each change:

1. Read the season's patch notes on ea.com
   (<https://www.ea.com/games/apex-legends/news>), section **WEAPONS** and
   **LOOT**, and EA's weapons guide (link above).
2. A new gun goes at the end of its class with its id
   (`<class>.<slug of name>`, game-data/README.md), `name`, `from` (the season
   it arrived, or `null`), `sources`, `ammo`, `uncertain: null`. A renamed gun
   keeps its id and gets the new name; the old one goes into `aliases`.
3. Set `asOf` to today and `season` to the season now live.
4. Run `node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js`; rebuild the exe and run
   `node dashboard/tools/sync-mobile.js`.
